# OPTIONAL — you usually do NOT need this file.
#
# With no .env, the app derives the API host from the machine that served the
# Metro bundle, so `npx expo start` works on a simulator and on a physical
# device over Wi-Fi with zero configuration. That is the recommended setup.
#
# Only create mobile/.env to point the app at a DIFFERENT machine than the one
# running Metro. If you do, put YOUR OWN address here — copying the line below
# verbatim will break every request, including login and the station picker,
# because the placeholder host does not exist on your network.
#
# Find your address:  ipconfig getifaddr en0
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<YOUR-LAN-IP>:4000/api
#
# For EAS builds a .env file is NOT uploaded — set the value in eas.json under
# build.<profile>.env instead.
